id: pm-rl-confined-sdk-locks
title: Provide descriptor-relative SDK lock acquisition before claiming state confinement
description: "SDK 2026.11.2 closes the original PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3 mkdir reproduction and refuses pre-existing symlinked locks directories. This branch adopts that release, translates lock_path_unsafe/4 to rl_state_path_invalid/2, and includes native regressions plus an old-pin failure proof. A later real locks-directory substitution at open(wx) still leaves an empty outside lock before refusing. The published SDK explicitly retains that stray file, so the original no-follow/no-outside-write acceptance criteria remain unsatisfied and the P1 stays open."
type: Task
pm_format_version: 2
status: blocked
priority: 1
tags[6]: blocking,filesystem,"gh:unbraind/pm-cli#1647","gh:unbraind/pm-rl#107",sdk-gap,"upstream:pm-cli#1647"
created_at: "2026-11-01T07:42:57.963Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-02T06:03:14.406Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Acquire, fence, release, stale cleanup owner writes and recovery audit writes operate through no-follow component handles, or refuse with a typed unsupported/boundary code before following an unsafe path.; Real filesystem regressions swap root, locks, cleanup gate and recovery directory at use; outside bytes and directory entries remain unchanged; ordinary roots and symlinked ancestors above the root retain released behavior.; Preserve native SDK token, stale-owner and fenced-lease semantics without a second hand-written lock protocol or process-global filesystem monkeypatch; regressions fail on revert."
parent: pm-rl-review107cubic
blocked_reason: Published SDK 2026.11.2 detects a late locks-directory replacement but retains the empty lock created outside the tracker. Original no-follow/no-outside-write acceptance remains unsatisfied.
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-01T10:09:22.335Z",codex-agent,"Public API audit: node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/core/lock/lock.d.ts:109,118 expose acquireLock(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...) and acquireLockLease(pmRoot:string, id:string, ...), with no directory handle or filesystem capability parameter. sdk/workspace-transaction.d.ts:43-63 likewise accepts a string pmRoot and no filesystem provider. Native stale cleanup opens its owner path after awaited pathname operations. The latest inspected public SDK has the same limitation. Upstream issue search for symlink lock returned no matching open issue; no issue was filed. pm-cli#1620 concerns ordinary writers and is not evidence of path confinement. This dependency remains an unresolved blocking P1, not an approved scope deferral."
  "2026-11-01T18:27:41.143Z",codex-agent,"Upstream acquisition race is now tracked by unbraind/pm-cli#1647. This supersedes only the earlier issue-search result, not the API audit or the unresolved safety limitation. README, decision-evidence documentation and state-boundary API comments now say pm-rl confines its own reads/writes while SDK lock acquisition confinement remains dependent on #1647; no pathname-only workaround was added. The follow-up remains open and unclaimed."
  "2026-11-02T05:42:26.971Z",codex-sol,"Started from pulled head 4d98fdb and read PR 107 plus cubic thread PRRT_kwDOTqJmqs6yXRp3. Registry reports SDK 2026.11.2 published 2026-11-02T05:26:13.578Z; its Security changelog names GH-1647. Plan: refresh dev/peer/manifest pins and both lockfiles, map lock_path_unsafe to the package boundary refusal, add native acquisition and command regressions with an old-SDK negative control, restore evidence-backed documentation, and run focused coverage plus requested gates. Published lock-confinement declarations say a lock created during a late directory replacement is deliberately retained outside the tracker; that differs from the supplied removal precondition and must be reproduced before claiming the broader original acceptance criteria."
  "2026-11-02T05:47:57.602Z",codex-sol,"Published-SDK behavior is now reproduced in test/sdk-lock-confinement.test.ts: raw acquireLock/acquireLockLease refuse static locks symlinks with lock_path_unsafe/4; all three package acquisition paths refuse the original mkdir substitution with rl_state_path_invalid/2 and leave no outside lock. A second real fs/promises interleaving replaces locks immediately at open(wx): SDK 2026.11.2 refuses with lock_path_unsafe/4 but leaves confined.lock outside, zero bytes. Its own lock-confinement declarations explicitly retain that file because pathname unlink could remove an unrelated replacement. Therefore the supplied stray-removal precondition is false and the original broader no-follow/no-outside-write acceptance cannot honestly be completed. Keeping that criterion open while finishing the bounded adoption and verification."
  "2026-11-02T05:56:53.258Z",codex-sol,"Final focused Node 26 run uses the exact runGate command linked on this item with source scope state-boundary.ts and test/state-boundary.test.ts plus test/sdk-lock-confinement.test.ts: 20/20 pass, no skips, 230/230 lines, 166/166 branches, 34/34 functions and 166/166 V8 statements (100% in every dimension). The native command matrix covers rl env register, rl run start/log/finish, rl generation register and rl checkpoint gc. The regression-only PM-linked run on the parent passes 8/8. The manifest contract command node --test --test-name-pattern=\"shipped extension activates\" test/index.test.ts passes 1/1. Requested npm run check, npm run lint, npm run docstring, npm run build:test and npm run changelog:check all pass; zero duplication across 58 sources, 523 documented declarations. Acceptance assessment: unsafe pre-existing locks and the original mkdir substitution are fixed and old-pin sensitive; native release/fence/successor and symlinked-ancestor controls pass. Original AC1/AC2 remain unmet for the later-open outside file, so the acceptance criteria and P1 are not closed. Exhaustive command-specific fixtures beyond the six-command matrix are not claimed; all native mutations route through the shared identifier client and acquisition boundaries."
  "2026-11-02T05:58:23.215Z",codex-sol,"PM-linked coverage initially hit the existing pm-rl-warf sandbox collision in an inherited fixture that initializes a tracker without an explicit root: 19/20 tests passed, while init_existing_settings_requires_force stopped the alias-history case. This is separate from the direct Node 26 20/20 and four-dimension 100% pass. Updated only the linked coverage execution metadata to pm_context_mode=none and workspace_context_mode=snapshot, matching the existing parent test convention, so current uncommitted source is tested in a disposable source snapshot without implicit tracker redirection. No production or fixture behavior was changed for the runner. Strict pm health with required merge drivers passes, retaining one pre-existing provenance advisory."
  "2026-11-02T05:58:54.199Z",codex-sol,"The corrected PM-linked snapshot run now passes 20/20 with state-boundary.ts at 100% lines, branches, functions and statements, no skips, and exit 0. This confirms the direct final-source result while avoiding the pre-existing tracker-redirection collision. Linked command and execution modes are retained in tests metadata. Final tree passes check, explicit lint, docstring, build:test, changelog:check and strict health with required merge drivers. Preparing the single authorized push with code, both lockfiles, documentation, this item and its history together. CI will run against the pushed head at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/pull/107/checks; full-suite success is not claimed locally. Original broad acquisition acceptance remains blocked on the demonstrated late-open empty outside lock."
  "2026-11-02T06:03:14.383Z",claude-orchestrator,"Orchestrator 2026-11-02: filed the remaining late-open window upstream as unbraind/pm-cli#1652 (SDK refuses lock_path_unsafe but leaves its empty lock file in the swap target). README now cites #1652 and no longer calls the retention deliberate, which the published code does not establish. The acceptance stays open until a pm-cli release fixes #1652; the characterization test in test/sdk-lock-confinement.test.ts must then flip to assert that no outside file remains."
